  "definition": "Margin of Error is the half-width that quantifies sampling uncertainty around a point estimate, commonly computed as a critical value multiplied by a standard error. It is used in Survey Estimation. It is commonly considered alongside Confidence Interval, Point Estimation.",
  "intuition": "Think of Margin of Error as a summary number: it compresses many outcomes into one interpretable value so you can compare models or decisions.",
